  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The sound of Arabic lāḏa invites comparison, but Lane’s usual sense is seeking refuge or protection (p. 2680). That meaning gives little support for the Hebrew ethical sense.\n\nGenesis describes the wood. The identification of the tree as almond rests chiefly on the Aramaic, Syriac and Arabic plant names. The city Luz, later called Bethel, is a proper name whose origin the narrative does not explain.\n\nMerged from `luz`, `luz-almond` on 2026-11-20: one root, one entry."
